1
00:02:12,520 --> 00:02:16,380
CONVERSATION 1
Hi Alan, sorry for not calling you back sooner.

2
00:02:16,380 --> 00:02:20,020
You said on the phone you had something you needed to discuss with me?

3
00:02:20,020 --> 00:02:25,500
Well, to get right down to it, I'm having second thoughts about my major.

4
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:36,600
With my family situation getting more complicated, and the end of my university education nearing, persisting with art history just doesn't seem the right choice.

5
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:44,680
Alan, in the last three years, I have heard nothing but how passionate you are about the art history program.

6
00:02:44,680 --> 00:02:51,260
You often told fellow classmates how fabulous the instructors were, and that you finally felt accepted.

7
00:02:51,260 --> 00:02:54,080
What would cause you to abandon it?

8
00:02:54,080 --> 00:03:04,680
My father's current financial situation has helped me realize that a more financially viable employment opportunity is not necessarily a bad thing.

9
00:03:04,680 --> 00:03:11,860
Art history nourishes my soul, but does nothing to put food on my plate.

10
00:03:11,860 --> 00:03:15,940
What about all the work opportunities I discussed with you last month?

11
00:03:15,940 --> 00:03:24,820
Have you gone to those places of business to investigate whether any legitimate positions might be available for someone with your background?

12
00:03:24,820 --> 00:03:25,380
Um, well...

13
00:03:25,380 --> 00:03:33,520
Look, Alan, if your heart is set on working in the art industry, you need to be more assertive and start talking with people.

14
00:03:33,520 --> 00:03:39,960
Networking is key if you want to become a celebrity in the world of museums and galleries.

15
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:42,840
Time is a very precious commodity right now.

16
00:03:42,840 --> 00:03:45,260
My social life does not exist.

17
00:03:45,260 --> 00:03:51,560
I can barely keep up with my studies and thesis is due by the end of this year.

18
00:03:51,560 --> 00:03:56,720
When can I find time to research jobs when I have so much to do as it is?

19
00:03:56,720 --> 00:04:00,900
What you do now will determine your future options.

20
00:04:00,900 --> 00:04:05,540
Now is the optimum time to put forth your best effort.

21
00:04:05,540 --> 00:04:08,940
I will take what you said into consideration.

22
00:04:08,940 --> 00:04:17,900
The advice is much appreciated.

23
00:04:17,900 --> 00:04:35,200
