00:05:28,980 --> 00:05:33,480
CONVERSATION 2
Have you decided yet what your end of semester business project will be on?

28
00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:35,840
Yes, how about you?

29
00:05:35,840 --> 00:05:37,760
Yes, go on.

30
00:05:37,760 --> 00:05:39,100
You go first.

31
00:05:39,100 --> 00:05:41,820
I'm going to do it about beef.

32
00:05:41,820 --> 00:05:42,380
Beef?

33
00:05:42,380 --> 00:05:43,940
Yeah, beef.

34
00:05:43,940 --> 00:05:51,000
I'm going to design a business case study for a cow farm that supplies beef for the domestic market.

35
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:54,620
Wow, that sounds very interesting and original.

36
00:05:54,620 --> 00:05:56,260
Where ever did you get that idea?

37
00:05:56,260 --> 00:05:59,220
I don't know, it just came to me I guess.

38
00:05:59,220 --> 00:06:00,140
But think about it.

39
00:06:00,140 --> 00:06:04,900
Beef consumption has been rising strongly over the past 20 years.

40
00:06:04,900 --> 00:06:12,480
As the economy continues to grow, consumer demand is expected to continue to increase, for the foreseeable future.

41
00:06:12,480 --> 00:06:17,900
And currently, most of the beef is imported, which brings with it added fees.

42
00:06:17,900 --> 00:06:20,560
So why not raise cattle here?

43
00:06:20,560 --> 00:06:22,020
Of course.

44
00:06:22,020 --> 00:06:23,580
Makes perfect sense.

45
00:06:23,580 --> 00:06:31,340
There's plenty of land out west, so if done right, it should be very profitable to raise our own cattle.

46
00:06:31,340 --> 00:06:33,100
Exactly.

47
00:06:33,100 --> 00:06:36,040
Seriously, that sounds like a great idea.

48
00:06:36,040 --> 00:06:40,060
You should genuinely look into it once we get our degrees.

49
00:06:40,060 --> 00:06:40,940
Thanks.

50
00:06:40,940 --> 00:06:42,580
So, your turn now.

51
00:06:42,580 --> 00:06:45,020
What are you doing your case study on?

52
00:06:45,020 --> 00:06:51,680
I was thinking about a car wash, but it now seems like such a boring notion after hearing your brilliant idea.

53
00:06:51,680 --> 00:06:52,480
That's cool.

54
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:53,500
I could see that working.

55
00:06:53,500 --> 00:06:59,800
After all, there's plenty of cars about, and those aren't going away anytime soon.

56
00:06:59,800 --> 00:07:04,320
While many people don't care how their car looks, many other people do.

57
00:07:04,320 --> 00:07:07,700
You've got yourself a vast and continual market.

58
00:07:07,700 --> 00:07:09,120
Right.

59
00:07:09,120 --> 00:07:12,980
So the idea is a large, self cleaning car wash.

60
00:07:12,980 --> 00:07:17,300
But I mean really big and well outfitted, like they have in America.

61
00:07:17,300 --> 00:07:21,620
I was thinking of having it cater to high end consumers in large cities.

62
00:07:21,620 --> 00:07:36,280
It could charge a profitable mark up by offering just a bit more technical equipment and professional service than competitors.

63
00:07:36,280 --> 00:07:54,320
