PASSAGE 1
Increased television time for young children has long been linked with poorer progress in some areas of development.

68
00:09:23,680 --> 00:09:29,500
One possible way to counter those negative effects is talking while watching the screen.

69
00:09:29,500 --> 00:09:42,800
As a new study suggests, the more parents engaged in conversation with preschoolers during TV time, the more likely those children were to have higher curiosity levels when they reached kindergarten.

70
00:09:42,800 --> 00:09:49,280
This was particularly true for children with socioeconomic disadvantages.

71
00:09:49,280 --> 00:10:04,460
"Our findings reinforce the importance of parent conversation to promote early childhood development and curiosity," said lead author Prachi Shah at University of Michigan Health C.S. Mott Children's Hospital.

72
00:10:04,460 --> 00:10:14,640
Researchers assessed hours of daily television exposure and frequency of parent screen time conversation among 1,500 preschoolers.

73
00:10:14,640 --> 00:10:19,200
And then measured early childhood curiosity in kindergarten.

74
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:29,960
The study specifically focused on curiosity levels, which are associated with enhanced learning and higher academic achievement in reading and math at kindergarten.

75
00:10:29,960 --> 00:10:38,220
And behavioral developmental benefits, especially for children from families with lower socioeconomic status.

76
00:10:38,220 --> 00:10:45,660
While many young children are now growing up with digital media exposure through mobile devices like tablets and phones.

77
00:10:45,660 --> 00:10:53,640
Television remains a dominant screen activity, accounting for 72% of all screen time.

78
00:10:53,640 --> 00:11:02,860
TVs are in 98% of all homes, keeping television exposure a relevant developmental context in young children.

79
00:11:02,860 --> 00:11:15,920
Excessive media exposure, including television, can displace exploratory activities such as play and parent child interactions, which are believed to be key to cultivating curiosity in kids.

80
00:11:15,920 --> 00:11:37,160
Our findings suggest the importance of parents finding opportunities to foster conversational exchanges in daily routines with their young children, including while watching television, Shah said.

81
00:11:37,160 --> 00:11:55,340
Q9. What do we learn from a new study about young children?

82
00:11:55,340 --> 00:12:13,460
Q10. What did Prachi Shah's study specifically focus on?

83
00:12:13,460 --> 00:12:34,180
Q11. What does the passage say about excessive media exposure?

84
00:12:34,180 --> 00:12:38,080
PASSAGE 2
Humans are aspirational, goal seeking beings.

85
00:12:38,080 --> 00:12:41,780
Each of us, according to research, has an inborn drive to acquire.

86
00:12:41,780 --> 00:12:57,860
The dark side of this drive to acquire is being mindlessly driven to possess more and more things and to socially compare our stuff with all the stuff other people have in their lives.

87
00:12:57,860 --> 00:13:08,540
So the question is, how do we ensure we tap into our drive to acquire in positive ways that will benefit our well being?

88
00:13:08,540 --> 00:13:13,360
One way is to become more intentionally aspirational.

89
00:13:13,360 --> 00:13:23,380
To be intentionally aspirational includes consciously aspiring to be the person you need to be to succeed in your professional and personal life.

90
00:13:23,380 --> 00:13:32,440
It also includes consciously aspiring to acquire things in your life that will positively impact your sense of well being.

91
00:13:32,440 --> 00:13:46,560
If you're not consciously, mindfully, and intentionally harnessing your inborn drive to acquire, you might be mindlessly pursuing all the wrong things.

92
00:13:46,560 --> 00:14:02,640
While your intentional, aspirational goals will include the pursuit of acquiring things that will increase your sense of well being, they ought to also include goals to help other people in your various life roles.

93
00:14:02,640 --> 00:14:14,540
Your intentional, aspirational goals will also include striving to be your personal best, a person of good character, integrity, and trustworthiness.

94
00:14:14,540 --> 00:14:20,160
Think about this from a practical rather than theoretical viewpoint.

95
00:14:20,160 --> 00:14:26,720
If you're not pursuing intentional aspirational goals, you have nothing to strive for.

96
00:14:26,720 --> 00:14:53,282
If you have nothing to strive for, you're putting yourself in the dangerous position of simply drifting through life, and you'll not be able to experience, live, and enjoy all that life has to offer.

97
00:14:53,282 --> 00:15:08,460
Q12. What is the dark side of our inborn drive to acquire?

98
00:15:08,460 --> 00:15:27,580
Q13. What might happen if we do not harness our inborn drive to acquire?

99
00:15:27,580 --> 00:15:47,140
Q14. What does the passage say about our intentional aspirational goals?

100
00:15:47,140 --> 00:16:34,480
Q15. What will you end up doing without pursuing intentional aspirational goals?

