00:16:34,480 --> 00:16:38,360
RECORDING 1
It's revision time for exams and dissertations.

102
00:16:38,360 --> 00:16:45,380
The pressure is on, so you'll want all the help you can get to age your memory and raise your grades.

103
00:16:45,380 --> 00:16:52,880
As a nutrition expert, I want to say that eating well can make a real difference to your revision regime.

104
00:16:52,880 --> 00:16:57,400
So, what brain boosting food and drink would I recommend?

105
00:16:57,400 --> 00:16:59,760
Coffee can have numerous benefits.

106
00:16:59,760 --> 00:17:08,540
However, while coffee may make you more alert, Individuals can build up a tolerance, meaning this is short lived.

107
00:17:08,540 --> 00:17:14,280
Coffee can also increase blood sugar and eventually cause lack of focus and energy.

108
00:17:14,280 --> 00:17:17,780
It's also worth noting that people react differently to coffee.

109
00:17:17,780 --> 00:17:27,340
Some people can drink it at midnight and go straight to sleep, whereas others get feelings of anxiety after a small amount.

110
00:17:27,340 --> 00:17:35,700
Also remember that coffee from a coffee shop may be stronger than coffee made at home, so stop drinking coffee by 2 p.

111
00:17:35,700 --> 00:17:36,200
m.

112
00:17:36,200 --> 00:17:39,980
and have a maximum of two cups of coffee a day.

113
00:17:39,980 --> 00:17:44,140
But be aware of your own reaction to it.

114
00:17:44,140 --> 00:17:48,080
Whole grain foods will ward off hunger.

115
00:17:48,080 --> 00:17:51,800
Examples include porridge and whole wheat bread.

116
00:17:51,800 --> 00:18:01,820
Combining whole grain foods with protein will help keep your blood sugar levels balanced, which is essential for mood and concentration.

117
00:18:01,820 --> 00:18:05,040
Berries and nuts are a convenient and nutritious snack.

118
00:18:05,040 --> 00:18:14,260
Blueberries, like many dark colored fruits and vegetables, can slow down brain damage and age-related decline.

119
00:18:14,260 --> 00:18:17,160
Frozen berries are also a good choice.

120
00:18:17,160 --> 00:18:23,340
They are usually cheap, last longer, and don't lose their nutrients when frozen.

121
00:18:23,340 --> 00:18:31,300
But flavored and coated nuts are less healthy, as they contain added oil, salt, and sugar.

122
00:18:31,300 --> 00:18:37,180
Doctors often recommend taking vitamin supplements to top up on the nutrients you need.

123
00:18:37,180 --> 00:18:51,520
But I would say food should always come before supplements, and the key to getting as many nutrients as possible is to eat a varied diet, with lots of different colors such as frozen berries and dark green vegetables.

124
00:18:51,520 --> 00:18:55,640
It's better to get everything you need from food and drink.

125
00:18:55,640 --> 00:19:07,780
For example, oranges contain not only vitamin C, which boosts the immune system, but also fiber and other components that you can't get packaged together in a tablet.

126
00:19:07,780 --> 00:19:17,220
Don't forget to drink a proper amount of water, which can boost attention by almost 25%, and can elevate your mood as well.

127
00:19:17,220 --> 00:19:19,740
Finally, don't skip meals.

128
00:19:19,740 --> 00:19:34,200
Eating regularly will help keep blood sugar balanced, and feed the brain with the fuel it needs.

129
00:19:34,200 --> 00:19:52,420
